{{#> layout
  title='How Vocably decides which cards to show during a study session'
  url='/srs.html'
}}
  <style>
    /* Long-form explainer layout for srs.html. */

    .srs {
      max-width: 40rem;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding-top: 2rem;
      font-size: 1.2rem;
      line-height: 1.75;
      color: var(--v-color-emphasize);

      & p {
        margin-bottom: 1.4rem;
      }

      & p a {
        color: inherit;
        text-decoration-color: rgba(var(--v-color-primary-rgb), 0.4);
        text-underline-offset: 0.2em;

        &:hover {
          text-decoration-color: var(--v-color-primary);
        }
      }
    }

    .srs-kicker {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 0.75rem;
      margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
      color: var(--v-color-primary);
      font-size: 0.8rem;
      font-weight: 500;
      letter-spacing: 0.14em;
      text-transform: uppercase;

      &::before {
        content: '';
        width: 2rem;
        height: 2px;
        background: currentColor;
      }
    }

    .srs-title {
      text-wrap: balance;
      margin: 0 0 1.75rem;
      font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 6vw, 3.25rem);
      font-weight: 600;
      line-height: 1.1;
      letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    }

    .srs-intro {
      margin-bottom: 0;
      font-size: 1.4rem;
      line-height: 1.6;
      color: var(--v-color-body);
    }

    .srs-point {
      margin-top: 4.5rem;
      padding-top: 2rem;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--v-color-border-muted);
    }

    .srs-swipes:last-child,
    .srs-ladder:last-child {
      margin-bottom: 0;
    }

    /* The next section's top border closes it. */
    .srs-swipes:last-child {
      border-bottom: 0;
    }

    .srs-point-number {
      display: block;
      margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
      color: var(--v-color-primary);
      font-family: var(--v-headings-font-family);
      font-size: 0.95rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
      letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    }

    .srs-point-title {
      text-wrap: balance;
      margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
      font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3.5vw, 1.9rem);
      font-weight: 600;
      line-height: 1.25;
      letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    }

    .srs-swipes {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
      margin: 0.5rem 0 2rem;
      padding: 0;
      list-style: none;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--v-color-border-muted);
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--v-color-border-muted);

      & li {
        padding: 1.5rem 1.25rem;

        &:first-child {
          padding-left: 0;
        }

        &:last-child {
          padding-right: 0;
        }

        & + li {
          border-left: 1px solid var(--v-color-border-muted);
        }
      }

      & i {
        display: inline-flex;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: center;
        width: 2.25rem;
        height: 2.25rem;
        margin-bottom: 0.9rem;
        border-radius: 50%;
        background: rgba(var(--v-color-primary-rgb), 0.1);
        color: var(--v-color-primary);
        font-size: 1.1rem;
      }

      & strong {
        display: block;
        font-family: var(--v-headings-font-family);
        font-size: 1.1rem;
        font-weight: 600;
        line-height: 1.3;
        letter-spacing: -0.01em;
      }

      & span {
        display: block;
        margin-top: 0.4rem;
        font-size: 1rem;
        line-height: 1.45;
        color: var(--v-color-body);
      }
    }

    .srs-ladder {
      position: relative;
      margin: 0.5rem 0 2rem;
      padding: 0;
      list-style: none;

      /* The line connecting the steps. */
      &::before {
        content: '';
        position: absolute;
        top: 1.4rem;
        bottom: 1.4rem;
        left: 0.4rem;
        width: 2px;
        background: linear-gradient(
          to bottom,
          rgba(var(--v-color-primary-rgb), 0.15),
          var(--v-color-primary)
        );
      }

      & li {
        position: relative;
        display: flex;
        align-items: baseline;
        justify-content: space-between;
        gap: 1rem;
        padding: 0.7rem 0 0.7rem 2rem;
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--v-color-border-muted);
        font-size: 1.05rem;
        line-height: 1.4;

        &:last-child {
          border-bottom: 0;
        }

        &::before {
          content: '';
          position: absolute;
          top: 50%;
          left: 0;
          width: calc(0.8rem + 2px);
          height: calc(0.8rem + 2px);
          border: 2px solid var(--v-color-primary);
          border-radius: 50%;
          background: var(--v-color-body-bg);
          transform: translateY(-50%);
        }

        &:last-child::before {
          background: var(--v-color-primary);
        }
      }

      & span {
        color: var(--v-color-body);
      }

      & strong {
        flex-shrink: 0;
        font-family: var(--v-headings-font-family);
        font-weight: 600;
        font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
        color: var(--v-color-primary);
      }
    }

    @media (width < 576px) {
      .srs {
        padding-top: 1rem;
        font-size: 1.1rem;
      }

      .srs-intro {
        font-size: 1.2rem;
      }

      .srs-point {
        margin-top: 3.5rem;
      }

      .srs-swipes {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;

        & li {
          display: grid;
          grid-template-columns: auto 1fr;
          column-gap: 1rem;
          padding: 1.25rem 0;

          & + li {
            border-left: 0;
            border-top: 1px solid var(--v-color-border-muted);
          }
        }

        & i {
          grid-row: span 2;
          margin-bottom: 0;
        }

        & span {
          margin-top: 0.2rem;
        }
      }
    }
  </style>

  {{#> text-container }}
    <article class="srs">
      <header>
        <p class="srs-kicker">Spaced repetition</p>
        <h1 class="srs-title">How Vocably decides which cards to show during a study session</h1>
        <p class="srs-intro">Vocably is designed to handle extensive collections of cards &ndash; hundreds or even thousands. You never have to review all of them at once.</p>
      </header>

      <section class="srs-point">
        <span class="srs-point-number" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
        <h2 class="srs-point-title">Reviewing every card in every session doesn't scale.</h2>

        <p>Once your collection hits a certain size (say, 30 or 100 cards), reviewing all of them in a single study session is not practical.</p>

        <p>Thankfully, you don&rsquo;t have to. With the help of a smart sorting algorithm called <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SuperMemo" target="_blank" rel="external nofollow noopener">SuperMemo</a>, created in 1985 based on research on long-term memory, Vocably shows you only the cards that need reviewing &ndash; like new cards or ones you haven&rsquo;t studied in a while.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="srs-point">
        <span class="srs-point-number" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
        <h2 class="srs-point-title">Every swipe tells the algorithm when to show the card again.</h2>

        <p>Every time you swipe a card, the algorithm adjusts when to show it again based on how you swiped.</p>

        <ul class="srs-swipes">
          <li>
            <i class="bi bi-arrow-left" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            <strong>Swipe left</strong>
            <span>You don&rsquo;t know it yet. The card comes back the next day or soon after.</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <i class="bi bi-arrow-down" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            <strong>Swipe down</strong>
            <span>You&rsquo;re not sure. The card comes back the next day without losing its progress.</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <i class="bi bi-arrow-right" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            <strong>Swipe right</strong>
            <span>You know it. The card shows up again in a few days.</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="srs-point">
        <span class="srs-point-number" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
        <h2 class="srs-point-title">The better you know a card, the less often you see it.</h2>

        <p>If you swipe right again in a few days, the algorithm will push the card back further. Over time, if you keep swiping right, some cards might not come up again for years.</p>

        <ol class="srs-ladder">
          <li><span>New card</span><strong>Today</strong></li>
          <li><span>Swiped right</span><strong>In a few days</strong></li>
          <li><span>Swiped right again</span><strong>In a month</strong></li>
          <li><span>Keep swiping right</span><strong>In years</strong></li>
        </ol>

        <p>With SuperMemo, you&rsquo;ll focus on the cards you need to work on while occasionally reviewing the ones you know, helping you lock them into memory.</p>
      </section>
    </article>
  {{/text-container}}

{{/layout}}
